				- Wayfarers find Grozmok Stone -<br>
<br>
The Wayfarers Brotherhood has located the Grozmok Stone. <br>
<br>
Calliav Giniuar, a magician becoming known for his strange visions, is now studying the stone.<br>
<br>
"Our friend, Calliav, is researching the Grozmok Stone and believes it has some kind of magic that may impact our next journey,' said Morden Rasp, Wayfarers Brotherhood leader.<br>
<br>
The ship that the Wayfarers Brotherhood is building in Nedaria's Landing is well underway as well.<br>
<br>
"We're always looking for enterprising young Norrathians to help us out here," Rasp said.<br>
<br>
- Guard injured on Duty -<br>
<br>
Idia of the Songweavers Bard's Guild was recovering last week from an accident.<br>
<br>
Jakum Webdancer, a friend of Idia's, was in the guild house while Idia was sorting mail that had begun piling up.<br>
<br>
"The mail was stacked to the ceiling," Webdancer said." I'm not surprised that there was an accident."<br>
<br>
Webdancer said the mail began to shift and lean and Idia was unable to get out of the way in time. The stacks of mail fell on her.<br>
<br>
Fortunately, she was not seriously inhured. After two days of bed rest, she is again having mail delivered for the League of Antonican Bards.			</td></tr>
